  "step_3": "The decision reason requires attention to outcomes with probabilities below 20% and an adjustment of their weights. However, in this decision problem, neither lottery has an outcome with a probability below 20%, so the reason would not trigger any adjustment. The individual, in contrast, focuses explicitly on a 25% probability (which is above the threshold) and finds it 'plausible'—a subjective judgment not tied to the mechanical weighting rule. There is no evidence that the individual considered probability weighting, compared weighted outcomes, or applied any rule based on adjusting small probabilities. The information considered by the individual (25% chance of 3000€) is not the type of information the reason is designed to process (i.e., sub-20% probabilities). Furthermore, the justification is based on plausibility rather than a comparative evaluation of weighted sums. Therefore, there is no alignment between the information used or the justification provided by the individual and the structure of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
